{"annotations":{"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"LOCAL PROJECT KNOWLEDGE SEARCH ONLY. With Google Surf Auto Ontology enabled (SURF_RESEARCH=true), one local broker lets multiple MCP sessions query the same knowledge base concurrently and orders writes safely. Always use this tool when the user asks to find, recall, inspect, or search information already stored in project memory, indexed local roots, papers, codebases, plans, experiments, or decisions. Use query_variants for multiple retrieval angles in one call instead of opening terminals or calling this tool repeatedly. Query embeddings are batched, candidates are fused with RRF, graph expansion starts from retrieved evidence, and the primary query is reranked once. Only bounded query-focused summaries from that final ranking are returned; stored bodies never bypass this response gate. If one retrieval lane times out, the other lanes still return and meta.degraded_lanes identifies the partial lane; do not repeat the same query automatically. Uses exact, BM25, vector, and graph retrieval with automatic RRF fusion and configured E5 reranking; no separate vector or RRF tool call is needed. Keep default lanes unless deliberately restricting retrieval; filters.retrieval_lanes skips excluded lanes entirely. It never opens Google, a browser, or SearchApi. When the applicable condition is known, filters.assertion_context selects only stored assertions matching it. Omit the filter when discovering possible conditions or finding source documents. Use search or search_parallel only when new external information is required.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","properties":{"all_projects":{"description":"Search every active named project. Excludes Inbox and cannot be combined with project ids.","type":"boolean"},"filters":{"description":"Optional project, source, type, role, lane, and recorded-time filters. n